{
  "case_id": "2011-11-166",
  "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: DAVID M. NEFF, ESQ., Chicago, Illinois; on behalf of Petitioners. DEANNE E. MAYNARD, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent. SARAH E. HARRINGTON, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1129(b)(2)(A) provides that a Chapter 11 plan must be fair and equitable to a secured creditor that objects to it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under subsection (ii), the plan must allow the creditor to credit bid when its asset is being sold free of its lien."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But under subsection (iii), the plan must provide the creditor with the indubitable equivalent of its secured claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The debtors have chosen to pursue a plan -- a plan sale without credit bidding under subsection (iii). The plain language of the statute permits that result."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But how does one determine what is the indubitable equivalent of the creditor's claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem with allowing a creditor the right to credit bid under all circumstances is, in a case like ours, we don't believe we will ever get to an auction because no one else will show up."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It makes no sense to me what you are saying because, under all circumstances, the credit bid, unless the property is valued higher than the credit bid amount, but then another bidder could do -- could make -- could enter that bid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, in accordance with (i), (ii) and (iii). I mean, I'm not saying skip those."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. NEFF",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NEFF: No, because you are going to have situations where creditors -- secured creditors will credit bid amounts that have no relationship to the fair market value, what we call, for instance, loan-to-own lenders, where their only interest is actually getting the title to the property. So you are going to have situations that -- where the credit bid does not equate to market --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: When this procedure is followed, how often does a buyer, other than the stalking horse, obtain the property?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: They tried and failed to prove what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is it correct that, really, the heart of your argument is that the real value of this property is greater than the value that you think the Bankruptcy Court would assign to it, if this were done under subsection (iii)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: When do you think, under 363(k), what's good -- what would constitute or has constituted in the case law good cause not to permit credit bidding? What situations have arisen under 363(k), where a court has found good cause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bankruptcy Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they tried to prove that in the bankruptcy court, and the bankruptcy court, at pages 43(a) and 44(a), rejected that as a matter of fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAYNARD: I think all those things are ways that it can happen, Mr. Chief Justice. And, certainly, counsel was distinguishing the -- during the plan sale requirement, where he concedes that, if you do a 363(b) sale -- you know, 363(k) applies, but he says it's not a problem because you can negotiate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: The Petitioner suggests that the usual rule that the specific governs, rather than the general provision, doesn't apply in this case because the specific is not a subset of the general. What's -- what's -- what's your view about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAYNARD: The for cause. So by reading in 363(k), Justice Scalia, it's not only the requirement of credit bidding, but also the only exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's the business value for upsetting the norm?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. NEFF",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NEFF: With regard to what courts have done for a very long time -- for the 30 years that that has been referenced have been primarily in section -- with regard to Section 363 sales, as opposed to plan sales. What it --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. NEFF",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NEFF: They could have gone under (i) if, in fact, that -- that the lender would have been precluded from making a Section 1111(b) election and also precluded from credit bidding because credit bidding's not required under subsection (i), and an"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "da13218405603df1a7fc2b1e96cec436383e9e59b2aff92780fdb8b38195600d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-da1321840560-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-11-166",
